    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file `score_image_safety.py` that checks an image for unsafe or policy-sensitive visual content using a concrete external provider, I will use the Amazon Rekognition service. This service is identifiable by the import of the `boto3` library and the use of the `rekognition` client. The code will include a function that takes an image file path as input, uses Amazon Rekognition to analyze the image, and returns the results. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866279609,
          "start": 1789866277692
